<BaseLayout title="About — Minted & Gone">
  <article class="narrow longform panel" style="margin-top:48px">
    <p class="eyebrow">About</p><h1>What Minted &amp; Gone is</h1>
    <p>Minted &amp; Gone is a static-first field guide for NFT marketplaces and their historical states: active, limited, inactive, dead, acquired, merged, rebranded, or unknown.</p>
    <h2>Why it exists</h2><p>NFT marketplaces change quickly. A warm registry can preserve what disappeared, what remains, and where users or assets went without turning the topic into a price dashboard.</p>
    <h2>What it records</h2><p>Records include marketplace identity, scope, chain coverage, status, frontend/contract/asset state, timeline events, source notes, confidence, and review status.</p>
    <h2>What it does not do</h2><p>It does not provide NFT price data, wallet connection, legal analysis, investment rankings, or real-time uptime monitoring. It is not investment advice, not legal advice, and not a real-time availability guarantee.</p>
    <p><a class="btn primary" href="/methodology/">Read methodology</a> <a class="btn" href="/submit/">Submit/correct</a></p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
